<h1>Interzone Science Fiction and Fantasy Listings</h1>

Interzone is a UK monthly publication issued in small-bedsheet format.
It not only has high quality stories, but also serves as a sort of 
UK version of Locus - with a books received section, interviews, and 
some of the most eclectic book reviews in print.

<p>
A one year subscription (12 issues) is currently $60.00 US, £32.00 UK, elsewhere
£38.00. Write:
<pre>
    Interzone
    217 Preston Drove,
    Brighton BN1 6FL, UK
</pre>
<p>
Or visit their web site at 
<a href="http://interzone.subscriptions.co.uk">http://interzone.subscriptions.co.uk</a>.
<p>
Most of the <i>Interzone</i> data was supplied by 
(<a href="mailto:redacted@redacted.com">Michael J. Cross</a>).
The anchors below lead to specific issues of Interzone; they
currently list works of fiction, poetry, and the cover artist.
